# AutoPulse engineering constraints

## SDK (Python)

- Never break the user's app when AutoPulse is misconfigured/down/slow.
- Keep hot path async/non-blocking with bounded queue; drop when full (document behavior).
- Use background batching with bounded retries/backoff; drop exhausted batches.
- Keep failure mode quiet by default; allow explicit debug mode.
- Scrub sensitive data by default; on middleware exceptions capture data then re-raise original exception.

## Backend

- Keep ingest endpoint fast and resilient; move heavy processing off request path.
- Authenticate API keys and store hashes only (never plaintext keys).
- Validate/normalize events and attach server metadata (project id, receive time, SDK version).

## Security defaults

Use HTTPS in production and conservative capture defaults (no full request/response bodies unless explicitly enabled).

## Implementation style

Prefer small focused diffs, keep naming consistent, and avoid scope expansion without explicit approval.
